hard_gates.evidence:
Plants: plants/apply-r11-plants.py; diff in plants/r11-plants-server.diff. The run is plants/planted-server-suite.log and plants/run-server/*.log: the full .NET stage through verify-slot, exit 1.

L1: GET /roles/{id} gets an endpoint filter with a captured dictionary. A 404 is then answered with any tenant's role that was read before. Caught by:
- G1HttpIsolationTests ('tenant A administrator (bearer) → GET /api/identity/roles/<B id> → 200: response contains tenant B marker');
- G1NonInterferenceTests ('8 answers depend on the other tenant's activity');
- G1ProcessStateTests ('closure ...RoleEndpoints.Map.roleMemo: a captured mutable ConcurrentDictionary').

L2: GET /users/{id}/access gets the same memo, held by a scoped service whose DI factory captures one shared dictionary. Caught by G1HttpIsolationTests (15 /access lines) and G1NonInterferenceTests. G1ProcessStateTests did not list it (see other findings).

Screen and API (walks/w1.txt, w2.txt; screenshot 05): a user made by keyboard with the Read-only role signs in with the set-up code and chooses a password. They then see:
- no 'New user', and Alt+N opens nothing;
- nothing in the palette for 'new';
- a record showing only Close, with 0 editable fields;
- 403 from POST /api/identity/users, POST /api/identity/roles and PUT /api/tenancy/tenant.

Escalation (attacks/escalate.txt): a helpdesk role holds users read/update/create and roles read/update/create, and works in ALN-DXB. Every escalation attempt was refused with 403:
- giving themselves Administrator, everywhere or in one company;
- adding resetPassword or tenant.update to their own role;
- creating a role beyond their own permissions;
- copying Administrator;
- giving Administrator to another user, everywhere or in their shared company, or creating a user with it;
- changing the Administrator's e-mail, deactivating, resetting, signing out, revoking with removePasskeys, changing the default company, unblocking or deleting the Administrator;
- deleting or changing the system role.
The bulk 'all that match' deactivation answered refusedBeyondOwn:1 with changed:0.

Revocation is immediate (attacks/revocation.txt): removing a permission from a role gives 403 on the next call of an already signed-in session. Deactivation ends the session (authenticated:false, then 401).

